{"id": "EUVD-2026-39323", "enisaUuid": "2afa3596-d03c-3da9-ba21-a11db8b1b340", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: phy: clean the sfp upstream if phy probing fails\n\nSashiko reported that we don't call sfp_bus_del_upstream() in the probe\nfailure path, so let's add it, otherwise the sfp-bus is left with a\ndangling 'upstream' field, that may be used later on during SFP events.\n\nThis issue existed before the generic phylib sfp support, back when\ndrivers were calling phy_sfp_probe themselves.", "datePublished": "2026-06-25T08:39:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:57:30", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/12fb84dc4dc8eb47ebe2b27f7de6255a4a205e1b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9326b654f90a09eadeb796c82801a5609d57f0c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a254779c169954fe23328a1db51f67be374f913", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0b27701ce93161d7bbf4b25fa20ca59963b0e20c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48774e87bbaa0056819d4b52301e4692e50e3252"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-53232", "GHSA-grrc-m4h5-r55j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.25, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "09306938-53f3-3cfa-847a-655764dc87d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "298e54fa810e027f1b0800d789eb862592721f08 <48774e87bbaa0056819d4b52301e4692e50e3252"}, {"id": "258e0a91-997a-36ab-b0e7-c2cd117f8799", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.143"}, {"id": "319e5327-27fe-3389-b549-8ec3d761d8f5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "298e54fa810e027f1b0800d789eb862592721f08 <9326b654f90a09eadeb796c82801a5609d57f0c8"}, {"id": "3264b62a-0176-3fa3-861f-01f538a5541c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.5"}, {"id": "3b596de7-cc10-365e-9d4c-1d2b430821c9", 